# MIRA build-context exclusions.
#
# This file MUST live at the repo root. The documented builds
#     docker build -t mira-base:latest -f deploy/docker/Dockerfile.base .
#     docker build -t mira:latest -f deploy/docker/Dockerfile .
# use the repo root as the build context, and Docker only reads
# <context>/.dockerignore (or a <Dockerfile>.dockerignore sidecar) — a copy
# under deploy/docker/ is silently ignored and .git, local venvs, and stray
# credential files get baked into the image.
#
# Pattern semantics: bare `*` does not cross `/`, so `*.txt` below matches
# root-level files only — requirements.txt is re-included and the
# config/prompts/*.txt prompt templates are intentionally kept. Junk patterns
# use `**/` prefixes because those files occur at every level.

# Git
.git
.gitignore

# Session scratch notes (never ship in an image)
SCRATCH-*.md

# Python
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
.Python
venv/
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.swp
**/*.swo

# Testing
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/

# Documentation (not needed in image)
docs/

# Development files
*.md
!README.md
.env.example
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# Data directories (app data is generated at runtime; user data mounts at
# /opt/mira/app/data as a volume)
data/
persistent/
firehose_output.json

# CI/CD
.github/

# Build artifacts
**/*.log
**/*.tmp

# macOS
**/.DS_Store

# Plan files
Plan-Ideas/
*.txt
!requirements.txt

# Local development artifacts
scratch/

# Junk
junk_drawer/
lazygit-master/
